{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:flat-map","title":"def:flat-map","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":989,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:flat-map","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:riemannian-metric]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:flat-map","line":1515,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Lowering an index]\n\\label{def:flat-map}\n\n\\uses{def:riemannian-metric}\n\n\n\n\nFor a Riemannian manifold $(M,g)$ and $p\\in M$, the \\emph{flat map} is\n\\[\n\\flat\\colon T_pM\\longrightarrow T_p^*M,\n\\qquad v^\\flat=g_p(v,\\cdot).\n\\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Lowering an index] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a666c61742d6d6170\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ariemannian-metric\">↗ def:riemannian-metric</a> <p></p>For a Riemannian manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(M,g)$\">$(M,g)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span>, the <em>flat map</em> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\flat \\colon T_pM\\longrightarrow T_p^*M, \\qquad v^\\flat =g_p(v,\\cdot ).  \\]\">\\[  \\flat \\colon T_pM\\longrightarrow T_p^*M, \\qquad v^\\flat =g_p(v,\\cdot ).  \\]</span> ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#ex:open-mobius-band","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:flat-bijective","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/cha